From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] input: add clipboard-copy-or-cancel key binding

A key binding that copies the selection to the clipboard when there is
one, and otherwise does not consume the key. Bound to Control+c, it
copies with the same key as most other applications (and as Windows
Terminal), and still interrupts the running program when nothing is
selected. The key is let through like any other key, so the program
gets ^C, or ctrl+c in the form it asked for with the kitty keyboard
protocol.

The selection is left as it is after copying, as clipboard-copy does.
Cancelling it would make the next press interrupt, and with an input
method (input-method-v2) key repeat arrives as release and press pairs
that foot cannot tell from new presses, so holding the key after
copying would interrupt the program the text was copied from. Typing
or clicking cancels the selection as usual.

Unbound by default. Requested upstream in
https://codeberg.org/dnkl/foot/issues/1333 (open), where the maintainer
found it acceptable if unbound by default.
---
diff --git a/config.c b/config.c
index 221258d..bc9a875 100644
--- a/config.c
+++ b/config.c
@@ -159,6 +159,7 @@ static const char *const binding_action_map[] = {
     [BIND_ACTION_SCROLLBACK_HOME] = "scrollback-home",
     [BIND_ACTION_SCROLLBACK_END] = "scrollback-end",
     [BIND_ACTION_CLIPBOARD_COPY] = "clipboard-copy",
+    [BIND_ACTION_CLIPBOARD_COPY_OR_CANCEL] = "clipboard-copy-or-cancel",
     [BIND_ACTION_CLIPBOARD_PASTE] = "clipboard-paste",
     [BIND_ACTION_PRIMARY_PASTE] = "primary-paste",
     [BIND_ACTION_SEARCH_START] = "search-start",
diff --git a/doc/foot.ini.5.scd b/doc/foot.ini.5.scd
index 8bedf45..cd1c485 100644
--- a/doc/foot.ini.5.scd
+++ b/doc/foot.ini.5.scd
@@ -1355,6 +1355,13 @@ e.g. *search-start=none*.
 	Copies the current selection into the _clipboard_. Default: _Control+Shift+c_
 	_XF86Copy_.
 
+*clipboard-copy-or-cancel*
+	Copies the current selection into the _clipboard_. When nothing is
+	selected, the key is not consumed, but sent to the application
+	like any other key. Bound to *Control+c*, it copies with the same
+	key as most other applications, and still interrupts the running
+	program when nothing is selected. Default: _none_.
+
 *clipboard-paste*
 	Pastes from the _clipboard_. Default: _Control+Shift+v_ _XF86Paste_.
 
diff --git a/foot.ini b/foot.ini
index 6469af7..197ea05 100644
--- a/foot.ini
+++ b/foot.ini
@@ -205,6 +205,7 @@
 # scrollback-home=none
 # scrollback-end=none
 # clipboard-copy=Control+Shift+c XF86Copy
+# clipboard-copy-or-cancel=none
 # clipboard-paste=Control+Shift+v XF86Paste
 # primary-paste=Shift+Insert
 # search-start=Control+Shift+r
diff --git a/input.c b/input.c
index f6ba9de..7bff59c 100644
--- a/input.c
+++ b/input.c
@@ -181,6 +181,17 @@ execute_binding(struct seat *seat, struct terminal *term,
         selection_to_clipboard(seat, term, serial);
         return true;
 
+    case BIND_ACTION_CLIPBOARD_COPY_OR_CANCEL:
+        /* No selection: don't consume the key (e.g. ctrl+c is sent as ^C) */
+        if (term->selection.coords.start.row < 0 ||
+            term->selection.coords.end.row < 0)
+        {
+            return false;
+        }
+
+        selection_to_clipboard(seat, term, serial);
+        return true;
+
     case BIND_ACTION_CLIPBOARD_PASTE:
         selection_from_clipboard(seat, term, serial);
         term_reset_view(term);
diff --git a/key-binding.h b/key-binding.h
index 4d40a66..8b3ba0c 100644
--- a/key-binding.h
+++ b/key-binding.h
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@ enum bind_action_normal {
     BIND_ACTION_SCROLLBACK_HOME,
     BIND_ACTION_SCROLLBACK_END,
     BIND_ACTION_CLIPBOARD_COPY,
+    BIND_ACTION_CLIPBOARD_COPY_OR_CANCEL,
     BIND_ACTION_CLIPBOARD_PASTE,
     BIND_ACTION_PRIMARY_PASTE,
     BIND_ACTION_SEARCH_START,
